# UIA-CORE-001 Rev 0.3.3 — Reference Implementation Plan (Rev C)

> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.

**Goal:** A testable, pure, dependency-free reference implementation of UIA-CORE-001 Rev 0.3.3 (identity, credentials, lineage graph, continuity assessments, conditional version binding / traversal, local acceptance) passing the full §12 conformance corpus A-1…D-4 plus property-based invariance tests — with traversal exposed as three independently testable phases, **immediate** merge closure as the only normatively implemented closure depth, and every semantic gap recorded as an ambiguity, never silently resolved.

**Architecture:** Pure applied-protocol library. All domain logic lives in `src/core/` as pure, deep-copied, deep-frozen (`DeepReadonly`), discriminated-union-returning functions with no Node-specific imports (portable to Deno/Bun/browser). Deterministic traversal via explicitly sorted, memoized path discovery → path validation → merge closure validation. Tests compile with plain `tsc` (no runtime TS loader); `node --test` executes compiled output. `node:crypto` is never used in core — a pure-TS SHA-256 is cross-verified against `node:crypto` in tests.

**Tech Stack:** Node ≥ 20, TypeScript 5 (strict, ESM via `NodeNext`). devDependencies (pinned exact): `typescript`, `@types/node`, `fast-check`, `eslint@9` + `typescript-eslint`, `prettier`. Test runner: `node:test` (zero extra deps). Runtime dependencies: **none**.

**Spec:** `docs/CORE-001.md` (UIA-CORE-001 Rev 0.3.3, Candidate Draft Normative). Normative keywords MUST/MUST NOT/SHOULD/MAY per §0.2.

**Revision history:**
- **Rev B** — edge-bound assurance; no invented conflict semantics (BLOCKED); three traversal phases; scope matrix; strict canonicalization; ownership semantics; explicit temporal context; rich result unions; mechanisms-vs-semantics section.
- **Rev C** — (1) unverified-claims semantics made explicit and spec-literal; (2) timestamp **trust kept separate from selection**: externally assessed `AssessedTrustResult` inputs, core never treats presence as trust; (3) merge closure split into normative **immediate** closure and **recursive** closure (BLOCKED, experimental tests, excluded from conformance coverage), with a minimal §8.6 clarification proposed; (4) scope × merge-closure internal contradictions removed — unresolvable cases BLOCKED, no synthetic convenience tests; (5) `evaluateBinding` receives `Policy` and `TemporalContext` explicitly; (6) B-4 error classification justified against the exact fixture (path-level failure recorded, closure-level code reported); (7) `DeepReadonly<T>`, and canonicalization hardened against accessors, symbol keys, non-standard prototypes, cycles, invalid Unicode; (8) compile-run strategy without a TS loader, Task 10/11 ordering fixed, Task 17 verifies per-case assertion classes.

